# Empire backup lessons (locked)

Every correction below was a hole in an Empire import, or a behavior locked after that import. The next backup, for this company or any other, must come in already corrected. Do not wipe a live company to retest. Apply the repair to the books that are already there, and keep the same repair on the import path.

Keep noting. Whenever a change is made to how a backup is read, how a voucher posts, how a ledger or outstanding is calculated, or how an entry or report behaves, add the next number in this file in the same sitting as the code change. Name the series and the column when the change came from the backup. Do not leave the change only in the chat.

1. **Work despatch pending.** The receipt's CHALLAN column is the job worker's bill number. The despatch it consumed is on each BILLDET line: ORDBILL (challan no), ORDTYPE (series code), orderno (despatch voucher). Link that line only to that despatch. Do not guess by quality, and do not spill a line onto the next challan. A line with no pick consumes nothing. On a new bill whose other lines already name their challans, an extra line with no challan (a sample received without a despatch) is saved and must not block the entry. The export must include those three columns. Check: Bhagwati voucher 20 (bill 57) is 120 pcs from challan 6 and 120 from challan 7. Pending before invoice 59 is **712 pcs on challans 5, 6 and 7** (112, 240 and 360). Repair: `repairWorkDespatchLinks`.

2. **State is the GSTIN, not the city.** Empire STATE1 is often the city (SURAT, JAUNPUR). GST state is the first two digits of the GSTIN. A place that is not a real state must not be treated as interstate. City stays in the city field. Repair: `repairPartyStatesFromGstin`.

3. **Sale amount.** Post the full invoice (BILLAMT). `finalamt` is after the bill discount. Do not store `finalamt − taxable` in `shippingCharge` and then post that as the sale. The imported discount is the V1 journal, posted once. A bank-receipt discount is credited only when no same-day V1 of that amount already hits the party, on the debit or the credit (within ₹1). Laxmi receipt 118 on 7/5/2026 has a ₹9 discount on bill 2025/F, and V1 voucher 10 the same day is Dr party 9. The receipt must not credit that ₹9 again. The party balance is 260142.

4. **Opening balance** (series 00) is the brought-forward figure. Vouchers before 1 April are already inside it. Do not add them again. A March bill's April discount journal stays; the March sale does not.

5. **Outstanding** hides opening journals, bill-tagged VATAV, settled returns, and unadjusted balances that a later receipt already used. O57 sales challans are not invoices.

6. **Bank and cash.** Voucher numbers are per series. Bills, discounts, and unadjusted picks on a receipt must be imported onto that voucher. Do not auto-pick unadjusted payments. Disc % fills Disc Amt from the bill amount. The default bank is the most-used account.

7. **Journals.** The opposite account list must include the imported P&L, trading, and asset heads. A journal whose party is a debtor posts on the customer when the supplier is missing. A new journal party asks to add the account.

8. **Work-bill discount and line amount.** DISCOUNT and billdis can be 0 while VAT was charged on a lower base. Bhagwati job bills are 12% off; recover that percent from gross and tax (`impliedDiscountPercent`) and do not also invent a second discount journal. Keep the imported line amount when it is not pieces × rate (P7 19, 120 pcs, rate 255, Empire amount 30090).

9. **Company-named series** stay out of general pick lists. COMPULSORY LINK stays optional. The pending quantity still has to fall when a receipt was adjusted against a challan.

10. **Cheque return.** FAS remark `CHEQUE RETN. ON` on a bank receipt (B1) means that receipt no longer pays its bills. The bounce is a separate bank payment (B2) dated the return date, remark `CHQ RETURN`. Re-presenting the cheque adds a new bank receipt with the same bills. The remark is already on the imported row, so the books that are already there release those bills without another import. Neither voucher is an unadjusted balance. Laxmi receipt 415 of 53260 on 17/09/2026 stays off outstanding.

11. **Work despatch category.** BILLDET.CATEGORY is the design on each despatch line (challan 232/L is FRANDY FABRIC three times: DARK BHAYA 240, BHAVYA DUSTY 300, BHAVYA COCO 180). A receipt line links to the despatch line of the same quality and category (O11 / P31). Linking only by quality leaves the other designs pending. The pick list shows one row per line. Repair: `repairWorkDespatchLinks` stamps CATEGORY from billdet, then allocates. Check: 232/L stays fully pending, and 225/L COCO BHAVYA pending is 149.

12. **Bill round-off.** Sale bills, purchase bills, and debit/credit notes post to the nearest rupee, including the Empire bills. The paise on those invoices (0.28, 0.16, 0.40) are the round-off. A receipt that is under ₹1 away from the bill settles it, so that paise does not stay outstanding and the party ledger is in rupees. Journals stay in paise. TDS posts to the next rupee (541.01 becomes 542) on mill, work receipt, and commission. Repair: `repairBillRoundOff`.

13. **Note picked on a receipt.** RECPAY can settle a debit or credit note on the same voucher as the bills. That amount is applied, so it must not come back as an unadjusted balance. Laxmi receipt 56 on 21/04/2026 pays debit note 13/D of 4057 with bills 1791/F, 1792/F and 1796/F. The note's own pending is the bank allocation; once that allocation exists the note is off outstanding.

14. **VATAV with one FAS line.** Series V1 usually has two lines: DISCOUNT A/C and the party. Nine vouchers (137, 138, 139, 140, 164, 165, 166, 168, 169) have only the party credit in FAS `code`, with the bill number in RMK. The missing side is DISCOUNT A/C, the account on every other V1. An empty opposite account must not become SUSPENSE for V1. The party credit stays. Repair: set that opposite account to DISCOUNT A/C. Suspense on these books was 4,766 DR from those nine.

15. **Less fold.** BILLDET.LESSFOLD is the fold on that line, on sale and purchase. It is copied as entered. The sale bill prints it as what remains of 100. A later import must not leave the column blank.

16. **Piece or metre.** BILLDET.AMT decides the unit. If the amount matches metres × rate, the line is MTS. If it matches pieces × rate, it stays PCS. The Empire voucher number is kept when that bill is opened again.

17. **Printed bill number.** Finish sales uses the number on the bill (BILLS.BILL), the digits before any star or letter. A voucher stored at 100000 or above is the same printed number. The series suffix stays on the series, not glued into the number the user types.

18. **Grey taka and mill receipt.** CHALTRN metres (WMTS, MMTS, RMTS, CMTS) are the taka rows of that mill dispatch, joined by CARDNO. Each MILLREC row keeps its voucher, mill, job rate, received pieces and metres, and the despatch it came from (CARDNO or DESPNO). TDS on that bill rounds up to the next rupee.

19. **Account heads and brokers.** Every MASTER row is an account under its ATYPE name: debtors, creditors, expenses, trading, and assets. A head used on a voucher but missing from MASTER is still created. MASTER.commission is the broker percent. A broker stays a creditor. PINVTRN.BROKER_CODE is the broker on the mill dispatch. Expense heads such as Travelling must appear on a purchase bill and on the journal opposite list.

These live in the software. A later backup does not replace them, and they are not rebuilt unless the user says that one is still wrong.

20. **Keyboard entry.** Enter moves to the next field. Enter at the end of a filled line adds the next line and focuses its first field. Two Enters on that blank line ask to save. Down, then Enter, on a blank line also asks to save. F9 saves. The mouse Add Line button stays.

21. **Sale bill print.** The bill prints as one full A4 tax invoice from its own page. The ERP screen is not what is sent to the printer.

22. **Open the voucher from the row.** A ledger or report row opens that voucher in edit. Back returns one step and keeps the party search.

23. **GST on entry.** A party with no GSTIN is asked before the entry continues. GST type can be Local, Interstate, or Non GST. Non GST sets the rate to 0. If the master has no GST and the user continues, the type follows the GSTIN.

24. **LR, rate, and photo.** LR number and LR date can be entered on one sale bill or on many bills together. The rate and cut last typed for an item are remembered on the next bill. A photo fill follows the sales type already selected. E-way and e-invoice stay as built. Poonam and Sunita e-way mode are left as they are unless the user asks to change them.

25. **Less fold percent and finish-purchase voucher.** Printed FOLD is out of 100. FOLD 95 is less fold 5 (`100 − fold`). Net metres = gross MTS × (100 − less fold) / 100. A metre line (MTR) is billed at that net × rate. The entry grid shows Net Mtrs beside MTS on finish purchase and finish sale. A photo stores the PCS column as pieces, the MTS column as gross metres, and the printed fold as less fold. Finish purchase (P2) next voucher ignores `typeBillNumber` ≥ 100000, which are prior-year copies. Aishwarya Fashion supplier bill 630 dated 18/11/2026 is finish purchase voucher 226.

26. **Work-bill payment.** A bank payment pending list includes work receipt bills, not only purchase bills. The Type pick is the series: WORK REC. LACE BILLS (P31) shows that series. A challan series is not a bill. Pending is the invoice minus that bill's TDS (TDS to the next rupee), minus a bank payment already adjusted on that receipt (`billType` work_receipt). Virendra Kumar Ashok Prasad Verma's lace bills 1–12 are settled. Bill 13 (46,752) and voucher 274 (15,589) stay pending.

27. **Sales order fold and bundle cut.** A sales order line has Less Fold and Net Mtrs, the same columns as a finish sale. Net metres = gross MTS × (100 − less fold) / 100, and a metre line is priced on that net. Bundles accepts `30*24`: 30 pieces, cut 24, 720 metres. A list with no star, such as `24.5+22+23.5`, is 3 pieces, cut 0, and metres are the sum. The typed text stays in Bundles. A later backup must keep less fold on the order line.

28. **HSN from the item master.** Quality Information HSN is the bill HSN. Korean Silk stored as 540752 must not stay on the series default 5407. Picking the item fills the line and the bill HSN from `hsnSac`.

29. **Sales order lines on a sale bill.** Picking a sales order copies each of its lines. Order 7 stays 20×24 (480 m, cut 24) and the 10-piece list (216 m, cut 0). It must not become one Korean Silk line of 30 pcs with cut 23. Cut is not rewritten as metres ÷ pieces. The bundle text of each line is kept.

30. **Sales A/C.** FINISH SALES and FINISH SALES (GST) credit SALES A/C with the invoice (the same figure the party is debited) and debit the GST on that bill. The imported VAT JV is the same GST and must not be posted again. A bill with no VAT JV, such as 1468/F through 1478/F, still shows its GST. Empire's GST debit on this account to 18/11/2026 is 23,40,829.53. The sale credit is the invoice, not only the GST.

31. **Bill discount is not outstanding.** The discount stays on the sale bill. FINISH SALES (GST) keeps BILLAMT as the invoice, and the line discount stays on the bill. `finalamt` is after the bill discount; an imported bill stores `finalamt − taxable` in `shippingCharge`. When that is below the GST, outstanding pending and the bank receipt pick list both drop that gap. A bill whose only remainder is the discount is on neither list. Shivpriya Silk Mills 23/F stays invoice 52,039 with discount 1,489; outstanding pending is 0, and it is not offered on a receipt. A bank receipt for a name that is also a supplier still lists that party's sale bills. A bank payment still lists the purchase bills.

32. **Sale bill discount shows on the bill.** The same FINISH SALES (GST) discount (BILLAMT − finalamt) is shown on the sale bill as Discount, and Net Amt is the invoice after that discount. The percent that makes that amount is shown in each line's Disc % column. Line GST is not recalculated. Saving the bill keeps `shippingCharge` when that discount is present. Shivpriya 23/F shows 1,489. Bill 998 shows 1,206 and 4% on each line. The receipt does not copy that discount into its own Disc Amt.

33. **Deleted expense journal.** After an expense bill is entered, Empire deletes the provisional journal. Series XX still keeps a copy numbered `271 J`. That copy is not posted again when journal 271 of the same amount is already on the party. A journal stored below ₹1 while its narration is the full bill is the same leftover. Make My Trip India: XX 271 J (5,188) and 292 J (18,398) stay off the ledger, and journal 307’s 0.10 stays off because purchase bill 318 already credits 7,083. The ledger closes at 0, the same as Empire from 1 Apr 2026 to 19 Nov 2026.

34. **Oldest bill first, and HSN on the line.** A bank receipt, bank payment, or debit/credit note lists outstanding bills with the oldest date at the top. The same date keeps the smaller bill number. Quality Information `hsnSac` fills the HSN cell on that item line, placed just before Bundles, on finish sale, sales order, finish purchase, and purchase GST. PURCHASE (GST GENERAL GOODS) has no series HSN. TICKET is 996421. P U FOAM SHEET is 39211310. Each line keeps its own code.

35. **Discount is not a receipt bill, and the line starts on Type.** FINISH SALES (GST) pending is the net after the bill discount, minus cash. Shivpriya bills 2, 23, 24, 37, 38, 39 and 77 were listed at 830, 1,489, 1,814, 783, 868, 781 and 804, each equal to the discount. Those rows are off outstanding and off the receipt list. The sale bill still shows the discount. On a bank receipt or payment the allocation row is Type, Bill, Date, Taxable, Bill Amt, Disc %, Disc Amt, Adjust, after Remark. Enter on Remark lands on Type. Enter on Type opens the oldest bills in the Bill column. Enter on an empty Bill asks to save.

36. **The receipt discount is an extra discount.** The bill's own discount is already inside the bill amount. Disc Amt on a bank receipt stays empty until someone types a further discount. After the bill is picked the cursor lands on Disc %.

37. **GST is on the discounted taxable.** FINISH SALES (GST) takes the bill discount off the line amount first. GST is on what remains. Shivpriya 998: gross 30,138, 4% in each line's Disc %, taxable 28,932.48, CGST 723.31, SGST 723.31, bill 30,379. The payable is that bill, not 31,645 and not 30,439.

38. **An unpaid bill stays pending in the year it was raised.** A date before 1 April 2026 does not pay the bill. Outstanding follows Empire's own paid flag on the bill, not the date.

39. **Empire outstanding is BILLS.paid.** paid = Y stays off the receipt list and off outstanding, even when this year's RECPAY has no line for it. FINISH SALES (GST) 393, 394 and 396 of SRI MAHABIR PRASAD KASHI NATH (28–29/8/2018), 933 and 966 (21/2/2019 and 26/2/2019), and MATA RANI FASHION 1001 (19/3/2021) are paid Y. SHIV KUMAR LAKHAN JI 1374 and 1375 (27–28/12/2024) are paid N, so they stay pending at 37,414 and 23,041. Of 942 finish-sale bills before 1 April 2026, 836 are paid Y and 106 are paid N. The import stores paid Y as `einvoiceRaw.empirePaid`. Repair: `repairEmpireSettledBills`.

40. **Each work-receipt line picks its own despatch.** WORK REC. LACE BILLS (P31) previous link is WORK DESP LACE CHALLAN (O11). The receipt CHALLAN is the job worker's bill. The line's challan is the despatch. The same challan can be picked on two lines when the prices differ, and each line's pcs come off that despatch line. A line with no pick still consumes nothing. Shivam Fashion voucher 275 received 240 at 52.80 and 240 at 52.60 from 228/L (one line, 882 KUNDAN). Both lines are on 228/L line 1, so pending is 402.

41. **Round off on every bill, and PAN from MASTER.PNRNO.** Sale, purchase, expense, debit and credit note, grey purchase, grey return, mill receipt, work receipt, and commission post the invoice to the nearest rupee. The paise are Round Off. Journals stay in paise. TDS on a mill receipt and a work receipt still goes to the next rupee. A work receipt whose taxable is 48,571.15 posts bill 48,571, round off −0.15, TDS 486, net 48,085. Repair: `repairRoundedBills`. MASTER.PNRNO is the account PAN. The export omitted it, so PAN No. was blank and TDS did not fill for a party with no GSTIN. The fourth character P or H is 1%, anything else is 2%. A blank PNRNO still takes the PAN from the GSTIN. Repair: `repairPartyPan`. The next export selects PNRNO.

42. **Party broker is MASTER.ADATIYA.** Selecting a party fills Broker from that name on sale, sales order, purchase, expense, grey purchase, work despatch, and work receipt. MASTER.commission is only the percent. The export omitted ADATIYA, so the account broker was blank and every entry made after the backup left Broker empty. 894 heads have a broker. AAROHI CREATION is RAVI BIJAY AGRAWAL. Customers store it as agentName, suppliers as brokerName. A bill that already names its broker (BILLS.BCODE) keeps that name. Repair: `repairPartyBroker`. The next export selects ADATIYA, and the purchase, grey, work, and sales-order imports store BCODE.

43. **Cursor after a pick, and Up goes back.** Choosing a party, a broker, a list value, or a dropdown moves the cursor to the next field. Up is the previous field. In WORK REC. LACE BILLS the first line starts on Challan. Up from that field returns to the header. Up inside the challan list steps back through the list, then leaves it.

44. **Poonam series move, 21 Nov 2026.** Sales orders 1–11 (SURAT SAREE PALACE through K JALAN, billed on FINISH SALES (GST) 1468–1478) are SALES CHALLAN (O57) 1468–1478. Those GST bills stay invoices and their order number is that challan. Sales orders 12–15 become 21–24, and FINISH SALES 21–24 still bill those rows. FINISH SALES (S1) vouchers 1–20 stay invoices. They stay on the party ledger and on outstanding. Each one is picked from the sales order of the same number (sales orders 1–20). The invoice is not removed. A pass that had copied them into sales orders 1–20 was reversed, and bank receipt 542 of SHYAM TRADING CO. on 14 Nov 2026 (41,825.70) again pays FINISH SALES 2. A sales challan is stored as posted, so saving one does not put it on the ledger. A later import must leave S1 1–20 as invoices and link each to the sales order of the same number. Repair: `linkPoonamFinishSalesOrders`.

45. **Sales type stays open.** On the sale screen, opening a voucher does not lock Type. Changing Type leaves that voucher and starts a blank entry of the new series, so another series can be searched without leaving Sales.

46. **Sales A/C credit is the Empire bill.** FINISH SALES (S1) and FINISH SALES (GST) (S51) credit SALES A/C with BILLS.BILLAMT, to the nearest rupee. BILLAMT is the gross plus LESSADD1AMT, LESSADD2AMT and LESSADD3AMT, plus the VAT. A less/add of −2% or −3% (remark D) comes off this credit. The cash discount in billdis, and ADD_AMT freight, stay off it. The party ledger, the printed bill, and outstanding stay on the gross invoice. From 1 Apr 2026 to 21 Nov 2026 the sales credit was 4,94,76,077 against Empire 4,93,26,101. Of that 1,49,976, the less/add still inside the credit is 1,48,857, and 1476/F adds its line discount back on top of the add/less (1,078). 1474/F stays 28,465 against Empire 28,424: its second line is one net metre (₹41 at less fold 5) higher, and its IGST is 1,355.46 against 1,353.51. 1475/F IGST is 1,331.11 against 1,331.12. GST on every other bill matches. The import stores BILLAMT as saleCredit. Repair: `repairSaleAccountCredit`. The next export also selects LESSADD1RATE, LESSADD1AMT, LESSADD2RATE, LESSADD2AMT, LESSADD3RATE and LESSADD3AMT.

47. **Finish sales GST picks the sales challan.** FINISH SALES (GST) (S51) previous link is SALES CHALLAN (O57). The Challan box was searching Sales Orders, so challan 1479 came back as "No Sales Order for challan 1479." The load and the party's pending list use the sales challan voucher (`typeBillNumber`). FINISH SALES (S1) still picks SALES ORDERS. The pick stays optional. A challan is already billed when a GST bill's order number is that voucher, or the bill number is that voucher in the same year and names no other order. Saving stores the challan number as the order number and on each line, not as a Sales Order. Check: 1479 is PRAKASH CLOTH STORE, five lines, still pending. 1478 stays billed. The import already stores O57 as SALES CHALLAN.

48. **One discount at the end of the bill.** A sale, purchase, or expense with several items takes one Disc % under the lines. Typing 5 puts 5% on every item, GST stays on that discounted taxable, and Discount shows the amount taken off. The line Disc % column can still differ. Dhara still fills the same percent when the party is chosen. Work receipt, grey purchase, grey return, and debit/credit notes already take one Disc % for the whole bill.

49. **Purchase account is the bill, then the GST.** PRINTING & STATIONERY A/C was only the VAT JV credits (180 CR). Empire debits the purchase head with the invoice and credits CGST and SGST back out, so the same account closes at 2,050 DR from 1 Apr 2026 to 23 Nov 2026. Every purchase and expense head does this from the bill’s purchase account (PURCHASE (GST GENERAL GOODS) P95, and any other series that names a head). A blank head uses the series Sale/Pur account. Grey purchase posts to GREY PURCHASE, mill job work to JOB CHARGES A/C, and a work bill (not a challan) to EMBROIDERY JOB CHARGES. The imported VAT JV is dropped on that head only when the bill already has the same GST on the same day. A journal the bill does not carry stays. Premware voucher 10 is debit 236, CGST 18, SGST 18. Vouchers 184 and 185 had no GST on the bill; the VAT JV remark still names TI/26-27/1989 and 2206, so those 18+18 come back onto this head. Voucher 277 stays 400 with no VAT JV. The party ledger is unchanged.

50. **New item on a sale line.** Quality Information is the item master. On SALES ORDERS, SALES CHALLAN, and a sale bill, leaving an item name or main screen that is not already in that master asks "Do you want to add this item in the master?" Yes opens Quality Information with that name (main screen, cut, packing NAKED, type FINISH, item type SAREE, selling rate, unit, HSN, GST) and the saved row fills the line. No leaves the typed name on the line. A name that is already in the master fills the line and does not ask.

51. **Credit and debit note numbers.** Empire keeps an older year at 100000, 200000 or 500000 plus the printed voucher. CREDIT NOTE (ON SALES) P91 voucher 500010 is 10/C***** dated 3 Jul 2021, ANAND SYNTHETICS. This year's notes are 1/C through 41/C, so the next one is 42/C. Taking the highest stored voucher made the next note 500011/C. DEBIT NOTE (ON SALES) S91 is 1/D through 5/D, next 6/D. Last year's copies are 1/D* through 13/D*. DEBIT NOTE (ON PURCHASES) S92 is 1 through 114, next 115. Older copies are 96* and 45**. CREDIT NOTE (ON PURCHASES) P92 has last year's 1* only, so this year starts at 1. The next number is the highest voucher below 100000 in the current financial year. A stored voucher of 100000 or more is shown as the printed number. The import keeps the raw VNO.

52. **GST on a credit or debit note follows the party.** CREDIT NOTE (ON SALES) P91, DEBIT NOTE (ON SALES) S91, CREDIT NOTE (ON PURCHASES) P92 and DEBIT NOTE (ON PURCHASES) S92 take GST from the selected account. The GSTIN state is the place of supply. The same state as the company is Local GST, so CGST and SGST. A different state is Interstate GST, so IGST. The GST % stays the series rate (5 on the sales notes). A party with no GSTIN is asked before the note continues. Non GST sets the rate to 0. A city in the account's state field is not the GST state.

53. **Note net follows the gross.** On a credit note or a debit note, typing the gross amount fills taxable, GST and Net Amt on that keystroke. Taxable is the gross after discount, other less, add and return goods. GST is on that taxable. Net Amt is the taxable plus GST, to the nearest rupee. A calculated taxable must not be sent back as a fixed taxable, or the next gross stays on the old net. CREDIT NOTE (ON SALES) P91 at 5% on gross 1,000 is taxable 1,000, CGST 25, SGST 25 and net 1,050 when the party is local.

54. **Ctrl+L opens the ledger.** On an ERP screen, Ctrl+L opens the account ledger over the entry, so the voucher stays. Esc or Ctrl+L again closes it. The cursor on Party, Party name, Party A/C, A/C Name, or Mill A/C opens that account. GSTIN, bill number, and party type are not the account. An empty party field, or the cursor on any other field, opens the ledger search. A name that is not an exact account stays in the search and is not replaced by the first account.

55. **Accounts and items are separate masters.** Masters lists Company, Accounts Information, and Item Master on their own. Accounts Information is the party (A/C Type, GSTIN, dhara). Item Master is Quality Information (name, main screen, cut, packing, rate, HSN, GST). A sale or purchase line still asks to add a new item, and that save stays on the item master. Clicking an item row opens that item.

56. **Item master dropdowns.** Quality Information packing, grey quality, type, item type, screen series, category and unit are lists. The export had only QUAL, so the lists never arrived. CATEGORY is the category list (DYED CUTPASTE, DYED JARKAN, 183 names). PACKING is BOX, CHAIN BAG, NAKED, THAILI, ZIPPER. SCREENCOMP is the screen series (BOX-1, LOOSE-1, P BOX-1). QUAL.CLOTHTYPE is the item type (SAREE, SUIT, DUPATTA, NET), not the category. Type is FINISH, or GREY when CLOTHTYPE is GREY. BASEQUAL is the grey quality (24 CARAT is RENIYAL), not the quality code. The next export selects CATEGORY, PACKING and SCREENCOMP, and QUAL also selects SCREENCOMP and BASEQUAL. Repair: `repairItemFieldOptions`.

57. **Sales goods return year.** SALES GOODS RETURN is series P3. A remark such as `[E:P3:100139]` is last year's printed number. The import stored the printed number, so this year's next voucher (the series max this year was 111) collided with a prior-year 112 and the add screen was a blank new entry. 28 prior-year returns were stored that way. A raw VNO of 100000 or more stays at that number and is shown with one star for each 100000 (100139 is 139*, 800023 is 23********). This year's series ignores those numbers. Opening 112 is this year's return. Opening 112* is last year's. The bill suffix column on P3 is blank. Repair: `repairSalesGoodsReturnNumbers`. The next import keeps the raw VNO when it is 100000 or above. A return already dated in the current year stays on its printed number.

58. **Geeta's SITADEVI return is voucher 112 on 24 Nov 2026.** The save of SALES GOODS RETURN 112 on 24 Nov 2026 wrote the line onto the imported row `[E:P3:100112]` and left the date at 7 Jan 2026. That is why voucher 112 opened blank and the SITADEVI line was not on 24 Nov. The line is SITADEVI, 1 pc, rate 688, amount 688, GEETA WHOLESALE MART. That voucher is this year's 112, dated 24 Nov 2026. Do not move it back to 100112.

59. **Cheque return puts the bill back on outstanding.** A bank receipt marked `CHEQUE RETN. ON` no longer pays its bills. The `CHQ RETURN` bank payment is the bounce, not a second payment. FINISH SALES (GST) 483/F of SUDRANIA TRADING CO. was Empire paid Y, so it stayed off outstanding after receipt 530 of 43,754 bounced on 6 Nov 2026 (bank payment 752). The paid flag comes off when that receipt was the settlement and no live receipt still covers the bill. Outstanding of 483/F is 43,754 again. A re-presented cheque keeps the new receipt's allocation, so the bill stays off. Repair: `repairChequeReturnOutstanding`.

60. **Bank receipt and bank payment.** BANK RECEIPT (B1) and BANK PAYMENT (B2). A sales goods return (P3), an unadjusted payment, or a credit/debit note can be picked before any bill. It takes its pending amount, and Net Bill Amt is the bills minus that amount. Rec/Paid Amt follows that net until the amount is typed. Cur. Bal. on A/C Name is the account ledger balance, the same figure as the ledger. ZOMATO EXP is an expense creditor: bank payment 757 of 3,287.78 is a debit on that account even though it is not a pending bill, so the balance is not left at 0.00 CR while the ledger is in debit. A slower response for another name, or for the wrong party type, must not replace the bill list or the balance. The list loads for the account that was chosen.

61. **Sale add/less, with a remark.** FINISH SALES (S1) and FINISH SALES (GST) (S51). Empire LESSADD remark D and rate −4 is the bill discount percent. Remark POUCH is an add, not a cloth line. Remark and Add/Less are one row at the end of the bill, not a column on each line. Shivpriya 966/F is gross 18,144, D −4% (−725.76), POUCH 2,100 (rate 21), bill 20,494. The 4% is Disc % on each line and the 2,100 is Add/Less with remark POUCH. A bill is changed only when that rebuild matches BILLAMT. 123 Shivpriya bills took the discount, including 966. 92 were left because the stored line amounts do not reproduce Empire's bill (1848/F* also has scheme SCH). There is no Shivpriya bill 1960. 1960/F* is Mahavir Textiles, with no pouch and no D. The next export keeps LESSADD1RMK, LESSADD2RMK and LESSADD3RMK with the rates and amounts.

62. **A bill discount is not a second journal.** JOURNAL (J2), opposite account DISCOUNT A/C. Saving a sale bill does not create a journal. The discount stays on the bill. RADHIKA SAREE CENTER J2/0317 of 2,510.80 on 14 Nov 2026 was typed on the journal screen (no Empire remark) and then picked on BANK RECEIPT (B1) 545. That receipt pays FINISH SALES (GST) (S51) 1078, 1093, 1156 and 1157, invoices 1,25,533.80, cash 1,23,023. Empire billdis and LESSADD on those four bills are 0, and the sale lines have no Disc %. The journal is removed. The 2,510.80 stays as Disc Amt on receipt 545, so the party is credited once and the four bills stay settled. The sale bills are not changed.

63. **The journal screen is this year's JOURNAL.** Series J2. TDS (T1), VATAV (V1), VAT JV (V4) and OPENING BALANCE (00) are stored in the same table and stay on their own series. The year chosen at login is the only year on this screen. Enter on the new number moves to the next field. J2/0329 must not open TDS 329 of KAIRAVADE ENTERPRISE, 10 Oct 2026, ₹42, remark `[E:T1:329]`. J2/0317 was the Radhika discount journal and is the only voucher removed. 318 to 328 stay, so the next number is 329 and 317 is empty.

64. **LR entry follows the type.** The LR screen lists the series in the Type box, between From and To. Changing Type loads that series. FINISH SALES (S1) is 24 bills: 1–12 are 17 and 30 Oct 2026, and 13–24 are in November. Bill 24 is PARI SAREE CENTRE on 21 Nov 2026 and has no LR. Bills 1–12 stay out of a list that starts on 1 Nov. A bill that already has an LR stays off while “Show bills without LR” is ticked.

65. **Outstanding selection.** Sales outstanding bills. Pending bills, goods returns, and a payment that is not yet on a bill are on the same list. Space selects the row under the cursor. Down, then Space, selects the next one. The checkbox stays, so a row can be cleared. Ctrl+Space keeps only the selected rows and shows the difference: net bill, goods return and the payment, and what is still pending. Esc returns to the full list and the ticks stay. Clicking a row still opens that voucher. Ctrl+Space is also taken when the cursor is on a tick box. The Difference button opens the same summary.

66. **Copy the outstanding pick onto the receipt.** BANK RECEIPT (B1) and BANK PAYMENT (B2). On the adjustment summary, Copy this entry directly to bank receipt/payment opens the selected unadjusted receipt or payment and fills the ticked bills. It does not save. GEETA WHOLESALE MART receipt 541 of 1,05,059 opens with 733/F, 751/F and 759/F filled. The 289 left over stays until someone saves.

67. **Work despatch item name.** WORK DESP CHALLAN and the other work despatch series. Item Name suggests Quality Information. QUAL.NAME is already on that master: FRANDY, FRANDY FABRIC and SATIN FRANDY. Typing frandy lists them. The screen had been a blank box, so the names looked missing.

68. **Work receipt challan left on the next line.** WORK REC. LACE BILLS and the other work receipt bills. The Challan list on a line shows what is still pending after the lines above. Pieces already typed on those lines come off that despatch line. When nothing is left, that challan line is left off the list. A line that took only part of it shows the remainder, with the pieces still pending. Picking the challan fills the line with that remainder.

69. **Old bill still open for the last 2 percent.** FINISH SALES (GST) (S51). SHREE VASTRALAYA & CO. Bills from before 1 Apr 2026 were received at 98 percent in the previous year. That receipt is inside the opening balance, so it is not on a bank receipt this year. Empire still shows the 2 percent: 1742/F pending 639, 1865/F pending 682, 712/F pending 567. Outstanding had the whole invoice and paid 0. The brought-forward receipt stays on the bill and is not posted again. A bill that already has a receipt this year is left as it is. A bill raised this year with no receipt stays at the full amount. Repair: `repairOutstandingBroughtForward`.

70. **Stay on the series, and the next blank voucher.** BANK PAYMENT (B2) and BANK RECEIPT (B1), and every ERP entry. Saving a bank payment stays on bank payment. The next voucher keeps that party, the same way a sale bill keeps the party. A/C Name comes before the amount. Typing a number above the latest blank opens that blank and says it is the latest blank voucher number. Alt+W opens that blank from any other voucher. Enter on a field selects the whole value, so a new party name can be typed straight away.

71. **After save, the same series stays on screen.** PURCHASE (GST GENERAL GOODS) and every other entry series. Saving jumps to the top, so the saved line and the next voucher number are in view. On expenses the voucher number is before the party. The next voucher keeps the series just saved: GST general goods stays GST general goods, the same way a sale bill stays on its type. The series is remembered for the next time that screen is opened.

72. **Transport is on the account, then copied onto the bill.** Accounts Information Transport. Selecting a party fills Transport on a sale, sales order, purchase, and expense, the same way Broker is filled. The bill keeps that name. Changing the account from abc to bcd fills bcd only on the next bill. The earlier bills stay abc. The next export selects MASTER.TRANSPORT.

73. **Account transport from the master.** MASTER.TRANSPORT is the transporter on the account. The first export did not select it, so Accounts Information Transport stayed blank and a new bill could not copy it. The 8 Nov 2026 backup has a name on 303 heads, and all 303 were filled. VARANASI TEXTILE MARKET is stored as PVT. LTD. and MASTER has PVT.LTD.; the space beside the dot still matches. Repair: `repairPartyTransport` fills Customer.transportName and Supplier.transportName only when that field is empty. A name already typed on the account stays. Sale, purchase, and expense bills keep the transport stored on the bill. The next export selects MASTER.TRANSPORT. The other MASTER columns were checked against Accounts Information. Already stored: NAME, ADDRESS1 ADDRESS2 and ADDRESS3 joined into Address, CITY1, STATE1 with the GSTIN state, MOBILE or PHONE1, GSTIN, PNRNO, PINNO, CONTACT, dhara, crdays, DRINTRATE, commission, ADATIYA, FLASH_RMK, MSME_NO, MSME_TYPE. ADDRESS2 is inside Address, so Addr. Line 2 stays blank and the text is not dropped. No box on Accounts Information, so left unused: EMAIL (32), PHONE2 (36), FAX (2), ADDRESS4 (0), bank name and account (4), distance (213; e-way still uses the PIN), CRINTRATE (1), TDSRATE (334; bill TDS stays the PAN rule), PURDHARA (22, and 21 equal dhara; GOPI TEXTILES is dhara 0 and purchase dhara 1). STATION differs from CITY1 on 14 heads. The bill Station is still filled from City.
